  "method": "Original newly authored source sheets and every final same-floor grounded inspection page visually examined; five neutral identities are first-column references. Technical registration is an independent gate. Fixed clip scale and whole-frame rigid placement only; no frame rescaling, source warping or substituted runtime artwork.",
  "direction_reviews": {
    "s": "All three final pages inspected. Frontal head, shoulder and skirt proportions retained. Static3 corrected to frontal foreshortened aiming. Draw, release and recovery retain two connected hands and one complete bow; released frames clear nocked arrow. Walking and moving attacks alternate supporting feet with narrower passing phases.",
    "sw": "All three final pages inspected, including all five replacement moving cycles. Near-right and far-left boot leading/contact positions swap across the four phases; bent trailing leg and narrow passing remain distinct. SWwalk97 uses four independently authored native frames from the same idle upper body, inspected individually and in full sequence. Static4 repaired; both hands, continuous bow/string and release clearance remain intact.",
    "w": "All three final pages inspected. Static2/3/4_v92 now preserve the idle/static1 head and body scale. All five moving cycles checked for opposite leading/supporting legs and continuous two-arm bow action. Native walk95 singles retain one quiver and show near/far leg exchange; visible arrow-feather count varies but no extra limb or missing quiver. Bow and released hands remain within frame.",
    "nw": "All three final pages inspected. Rear-side head, flower, long hair, leaf skirt, quiver and torso retain shape against neutral. Moving1–5 alternate the supporting heel and trailing bent leg; release has no nocked arrow (moving5 repaired). Two arms connect naturally around partly occluded torso and bow.",
    "n": "All three final pages inspected. Static1–5 and moving1–5 retain rear-facing hair/body with forward bow arm and arrow naturally occluded into depth; no horizontal arrow across the visible back or hands on back of skull. Moving5_v82 retains stable head/torso and alternating foot phases. Skill cast uses independent forward command and clean two-hand silhouette.",
    "utility": "Full final utility page inspected. Hurt closes eyes while upright, interact raises and returns the free hand, prayer holds a quiet hand gesture. Death lowers to knees and then an intact prone figure by intent; full head/hair/body/boots and bow remain inside the authored cell."
